WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.110
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.110
An overnight trip, huh?

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:32.760
Yes.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.980
<b>Nikkei Average Stock Price 
Recovering for the First Time in 3 Days</b>

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.980
VSP's stock price is...

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.280
How unusual for Kaya 
to make a suggestion.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:35.280
<b>Tour of Fall Flavors</b>

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.660
What huge mushrooms!

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:39.410
Apparently, they want 
to eat from the same pot,

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.220
Those look delicious!

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.770
By the way, I haven't had 
these mushrooms in five years!

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:43.790
have fried saury, raw saury, 
and saury dumplings,

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:45.700
After all, they're expensive!

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:45.700
and have an honest 
talk with each other.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:49.670
That's why they want 
to go to Kesennuma.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:49.740
Hey, Catherine. I can't have you 
featuring just the mushrooms.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.710
I've got lots of delicious things 
besides mushrooms like bonito,

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.710
Do they want to go to 
Kesennuma for the saury?

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:52.650
Yes.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.990
salmon, chestnuts, and persimmons.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.990
Also, Kaya's aunt runs 
an inn in Kesennuma

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:56.890
I know that, Steven.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:59.220
and will let them stay for cheap.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.160
Which is your favorite?

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.890
What's my favorite?

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.720
Oh, really? That sounds good.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.720
You, of course.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.970
But President, don't you understand?

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.970
Oh, you're always so crazy.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:06.650
What perfect timing. 
Saury's in season.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:07.480
Anyway, the king of 
fall flavors is saury.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:07.850
That's not what I meant.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.660
Matsuda, we'll go with them.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.330
Find some tickets.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.510
Understood.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.340
Oh, and you'll pay for your own.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:15.860
What?!

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.620
By the way, what happened with Nanami?

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.370
I haven't talked to her since then.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.800
Sheesh...

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.250
We need to do something about her, too.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.250
<b>For Tomizawa 
A train is arriving</b>

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:17.020
Kaya-chan, welcome home.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:18.510
I'm back.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.020
I'm so glad you're here.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:21.930
Sorry.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.880
Are these them?

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:24.580
Yeah.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.890
Nice to meet you!

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.680
Thank you for having us.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.640
Thank you for accommodating so many.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.800
No, thank you for looking after Kaya-chan.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.400
Come on in.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.650
Hasn't the city become beautiful?

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:38.840
Yeah.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.420
This year's saury is really good.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:42.680
I look forward to it.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.030
Saury!

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.450
Minami, you're drooling!

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:50.120
But we're not here to play!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:52.010
Let's go jogging before dinner!

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.290
What?

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.230
You're so mean...

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:58.640
But won't it make dinner taste even better?

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:11.210
Kaya, are you okay?

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:11.930
My shoelace...

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.770
It really has improved.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.030
What?

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:20.820
My aunt's right. 
The city has gotten a lot better.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:28.820
Has it been a while 
since you were last here?

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:31.330
Yeah. It's my first time since then.

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:35.790
I see. I was in Tokyo then, so...

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.080
Right.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.920
When I was little, I lost my parents.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:46.930
My aunt was my mother.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:47.970
I see.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:50.720
I caused her a lot of worry.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:53.590
Hey!

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:54.850
Are you guys okay?

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.990
Sorry! We'll be right there!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.120
Thanks for the food!

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:11.620
Saury!

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.750
It's really tasty, meow!

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.690
Kayatan, that's amazing.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:23.010
Kaya-chan has loved saury 
since she was little.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.830
Really? Lucky.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:28.260
Yoppi, don't tell me you don't like saury.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.590
I can't believe you don't like saury.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:33.320
Have you even tried it?

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.520
You're such a little kid.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:39.130
I just have to eat it, right?

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:40.230
You're supposed to squeeze some citrus

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.690
and put grated white radish on it.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.150
I know that.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:45.280
It's good.

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:46.530
Isn't it?

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:52.280
Does saury make your breasts bigger?

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.370
Oh, I see.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.540
Kayatan, you've liked saury 
since you were little, right?

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.540
It must be.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.790
Saury has nothing to do with it.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.800
By the way, where's the president?

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.310
This is on the house.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:19.330
Oh, don't worry about me.

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.000
Just because I'm a woman 
traveling through the north,

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.220
it doesn't necessarily mean that.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.570
Well, but...

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:25.790
Anyway, it's the opposite.

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:29.070
Lately, coming north gives me energy.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:33.290
Thanks for the food.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:34.360
Here's your money.

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:35.700
Keep the change.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.470
You're a thousand yen short.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:38.080
Oh...

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.030
Thank you very much.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.680
Now, let's see how these girls

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.840
will get themselves 
out of this predicament.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:06.750
What's wrong?

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:07.690
Nothing.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.890
You're really into this.

00:07:08.890 --> 00:07:10.740
Yeah, I run every day.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.740
I see.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.950
I wasn't sure what would happen then,

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:22.870
but everyone's stronger than I expected.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:26.710
Can I tell you a secret?

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.380
What?

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.720
Can I read it?

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.300
Yeah.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:38.410
Kaya-chan, how are you?

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:42.430
A buoy with a Shoutoumaru 
mark washed up in Alaska.

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.820
We decided to take it.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.800
Anyway, Kaya-chan, 
why don't you come home?

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:49.900
What is this?

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:52.220
I got that letter from my aunt last year.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:59.630
Three years ago, I lost 
many important things.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:03.040
Living here became really difficult.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.710
I ran away to Sendai.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:10.890
Anyway, I still couldn't go home, 
even after receiving that letter.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:15.180
I couldn't make the decision 
to return for so long.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:19.130
In the end, I idled around in Sendai.

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:22.430
I didn't know what to do.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:24.690
Then I happened to see it.

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:26.190
<b>Gyoza no Tenpari</b>

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:32.690
You can be a star!

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:32.690
Large Idol Group AUDITION Open!!

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:38.450
<b>Gyoza no Tenpari</b>

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:38.280
I thought I'd apply.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:40.700
I started on a whim.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:44.300
I thought I'd work and have fun,

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:48.210
and if it got boring, 
I'd quit on a whim.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:51.620
But it slowly stopped being that way.

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:54.470
With everything that's happened, 
it's just not fun, anymore.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.890
I've had frustrating and 
difficult experiences, too.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:01.470
And then I remembered 
something from my past.

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:05.480
I lost again!

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:06.930
You're so weak!

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:08.860
Why are you so strong?

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:13.300
I was sick of losing to my 
grandpa and dad all the time.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:16.090
While trying over and over, 
I gradually got stronger.

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:18.750
These days, I can almost beat my dad.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:19.620
Really?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.580
You should keep challenging people 
stronger than yourself, too.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.120
It'll make you stronger.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.500
Okay! Let's do it again!

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:29.000
Sure!

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:32.030
I kept trying after that.

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:36.740
By the end, I had improved enough 
to beat him a lot of the time.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:42.260
That's why I can't walk away 
after losing to strong opponents.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:47.340
I don't think Wake Up, Girls! 
can end like this, either.

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:51.450
I feel like I finally found 
something I can work toward.

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:54.690
That's why I felt like 
I could return to the city

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.770
I'd been running from.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:03.260
But I couldn't do it alone, 
so I had everyone come with me.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.660
I see.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:10.670
I don't know how that little 
buoy made its way to Alaska,

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:17.170
but I felt like it was 
telling me to keep trying.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:21.310
I want to work hard for those who can't.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:23.660
That's how I feel now.

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:28.110
This is my secret.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.440
Sorry. I know that wasn't like me.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:32.150
It's okay.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:36.080
I can't hear what they're saying.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.820
Let's get a little closer.

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:39.290
They'll notice.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:40.450
Quiet.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:43.550
Now it's your turn.

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:44.260
What?

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.780
Don't you think it's time to tell us?

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:57.440
Remember what you said?

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.050
Huh?

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.840
I want to make myself happy.

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:04.810
What did that mean?

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:09.680
There's something I've always thought.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:14.070
There are three different 
ways to make someone happy.

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:14.820
What?

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:16.280
Yeah...

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:18.210
First,

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:21.180
there are those who can make lots 
of people around the world happy.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:25.810
Then there are people who can make 
the people around them happy.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:26.830
Finally,

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:30.820
there are those who can 
make themselves happy.

00:11:31.970 --> 00:11:36.840
I haven't made the people of the 
world or the ones around me happy,

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:41.470
so I, at least, want to make myself happy.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:46.670
I want to make myself happy, too.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.470
For those who couldn't do it themselves.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.230
So, did you do it?

00:11:55.510 --> 00:11:59.410
Does that have something to do 
with the reason you quit I-1?

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.360
Everyone's worried about you.

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:08.930
It's a long story.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:11.750
Okay.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:15.250
<b>4 Years Ago</b>

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:20.010
I joined I-1 when I was 12.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.630
For two years after that, 
I worked desperately hard.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:29.010
You are the first generation of the I-1 Club.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:33.390
You are the elite who were accepted 
out of ten thousand applicants.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.240
Don't forget. Starting today,

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:39.900
you are an idol first and 
a human being second.

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:43.150
Make sure you understand that.

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:44.530
Yes, sir!

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.420
<b>Crazy About You</b>

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:58.420
At first, it was fun.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:01.960
Everything I saw and heard was so new.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:05.790
I made new discoveries every day.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:08.300
But eventually...

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.690
I felt restricted by the harsh rules.

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.560
It became harder and harder to breathe.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.470
I felt restricted and constrained.

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:24.320
But because becoming an idol was 
my dream, I kept working hard.

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:28.070
Starting tomorrow, the following 
individuals do not need to come.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:29.700
Number 16.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:37.150
I heard some pictures she took 
with a male friend got out.

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:39.840
Number 23.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.590
Starting tomorrow, you don't need to come.

00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:46.470
Number 37.

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:48.520
Starting tomorrow, you don't need to come.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.480
Number 5, starting tomorrow, 
you don't need to come.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:13:59.230
Serika?

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:03.110
I don't want to quit!

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:04.330
What?

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.440
I don't want to quit!

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:09.180
Why did you break the rules, then?

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:12.760
I'm always telling you romantic 
relationships are forbidden.

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:14.490
Why can't we love?

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:19.250
I've never neglected 
my work because of love!

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:22.990
I'm practicing my singing and dancing!

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:24.630
That doesn't matter.

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:39.150
Um... We worked hard together to get here.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:42.650
I think it was wrong of Serika 
to break the rules, but please.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.130
Please don't make her quit!

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:46.900
Number 3...

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:49.290
Your name is Shimada-kun, isn't it?

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:51.490
You don't understand at all.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:52.160
What?

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:56.780
You're only allowed to love your fans.

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.800
If you show even a hint 
of love with someone else,

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.490
in that moment, you stop being an idol.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:05.920
In other words, 
you're a piece of subhuman trash.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:09.930
Such an existence is not necessary in I-1.

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.550
Don't talk about Serika like that!

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:23.150
I am very familiar 
with how good you are.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.940
That's why I chose you to be I-1's center.

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:31.020
Fortunately, all the singles 
we've produced since you became

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:34.200
the center have reached 
the top of weekly charts.

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:39.000
Are you sure you don't mistakenly 
believe you did that all yourself?

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:41.500
Learn your place.

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:47.160
We will be releasing two 
singles simultaneously next.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.480
You will be the center of one.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:52.510
Number 2 will be the 
center of the other.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:53.770
Shihocchi?

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:58.040
If your sales are better, 
I will overlook this.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:01.770
However, if number 2's sales 
are better, you will be fired.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.270
You can't...

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:07.030
Shouldn't you be prepared 
for such consequences

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:09.660
when you complain to your employer?

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:13.530
I understand.

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:17.200
I'm always telling you girls.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:20.540
You're an idol first and 
a human being second.

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:22.580
No...

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:27.540
We are people first.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:32.300
We will be releasing two 
singles simultaneously next.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:33.050
<b>Mayushi VS Shihocchi Face Off!!</b>

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:34.050
<b>The loser is fired?! An intense battle begins!!</b>

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:36.210
What do you mean?

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:39.650
Why? Aren't you the one 
who said you wanted to do it?

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:42.030
Why would you go and do that?

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:43.440
But Serika...

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.050
Who cares about anyone else?

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:48.290
What are you going to do if you get fired?

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.790
I'll do my best to place first.

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:52.570
Do you really think you can do it?

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:55.320
I can't believe you made 
Shiraki-san angry...

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:58.590
There are some things you can't 
accomplish with hard work alone!

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:00.200
Mom?

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:05.790
I sacrificed everything for you...

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.960
This is all your fault!

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:14.350
I don't believe it. Didn't...

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:18.720
Shiho's single topped the weekly charts.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:19.470
<b>Staff fed up with I-1 Mayushi's poor conduct?</b>

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.220
<b>Secret meetings at night in Roppongi?!</b>

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:20.970
<b>Mayushi fired?!</b>

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:20.970
<b>I-1 Club 
Shihocchi becomes 
the new center!</b>

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:26.450
They did it to trap you.

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:29.980
Yeah. I caused trouble for my dad, too.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:33.790
That's rough.

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:37.780
In the end, because of my work 
in the entertainment industry,

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.990
my parents got divorced.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.740
I was fired from I-1.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:44.940
I returned to my mother's home in Sendai.

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:49.000
I've been running, too.

00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:54.460
But I can't give up singing and dancing.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:57.560
That's why I wanted to give it another try.

00:17:58.630 --> 00:17:59.760
I see.

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:03.400
I'd be lying if I said I didn't 
hold a grudge against I-1.

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:06.360
I've been traumatized by
 the entertainment industry, too.

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:10.040
But since meeting 
President Tange, Matsuda-san,

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:13.270
and everyone in Wake Up, Girls!...

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:16.000
I want to overcome that.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.780
No, I believe I can overcome that.

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:25.430
After all, I've learned a lot of things

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:27.270
I didn't know when I was in I-1.

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:29.960
I hope you'll support us!

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:33.040
This will make Grandma Isokawa happier.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.360
You looked like you wanted to join us.

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.510
Come on, then. Let's do it.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:39.300
If you could tell us what we 
did wrong, we'd appreciate it.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.010
I'll do my best.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:43.680
Come back, Airi!

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:47.830
That's why I wanted 
to stand on the stage again

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.190
with everyone from Green Leaves.

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:54.130
I felt like I was going nowhere.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:55.940
I see how it is now.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:19:02.450
I finally believe I'm here 
to make myself happy.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:07.240
You should tell everyone that.

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:09.240
They're really worried about you.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:09.960
What?

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:16.590
Yoppi...

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:20.050
I'm sorry for not telling you.

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:24.330
My stubbornness must 
have been a nuisance.

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:26.720
I'm really sorry.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:29.900
It's okay. I'm sorry.

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:32.350
I said too much.

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:42.380
I may not be much of a leader, 
but I'm doing my best, too.

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:44.870
So talk to me.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.620
I want you to talk to me.

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:50.730
Yeah, I understand.

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:52.250
I know.

00:19:54.780 --> 00:19:56.000
Oh, come on!

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:58.750
What's gotten into you?

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:01.320
This perfect two-shot!

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:05.140
I can't have you speaking 
so honestly with each other!

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:07.700
I'm going to stop with 
the half-measures, too!

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:11.260
Nanami, I've been wondering 
for a while now, but what is that?

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:12.270
Huh? What?

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.580
What?!

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:17.220
I, Hisami Nanami, declare my intention

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:20.400
to work wholeheartedly 
for Wake Up, Girls!

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:22.490
Hikari... Music...

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.660
What is this?

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:26.880
Huh? The Hikarizuka 
entrance requirements?

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:29.300
Does this mean you're not applying?

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:30.530
Not this time.

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:34.290
In any case, I'm going to 
focus on the Idol Festival.

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:36.000
What? You are?

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.330
I made my decision.

00:20:37.330 --> 00:20:39.180
You're on fire, Nanami.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:42.110
Now that that's decided, Ai-chan, 
you'll have to train hard.

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:43.050
Who? Me?

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:44.510
Your dancing.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:45.580
Honestly speaking,

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:47.950
what you showed me the other 
day was completely wrong.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:49.310
What?!

00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:56.190
You shouldn't litter.

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:59.310
Nanami, why did you 
have to scatter the pieces?

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:00.380
Sorry about that.

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:01.690
I couldn't help myself.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:04.590
Nanami, you got some in the ocean.

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:07.570
Oh, fine. I'll pick it up...

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:09.570
Watch out!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.310
Why are you making so much 
noise so early in the morning?

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:23.970
You can't be serious...

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:26.890
It's so cramped!

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:28.470
You need to warm up.

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:32.200
Sheesh...

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.550
Well, who cares?

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:35.320
What are they going to do 
if they catch a cold?

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:36.480
They have no self-awareness!

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:38.440
I suppose...

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.290
But I'm glad we came.

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:40.730
What?

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:46.600
People who didn't know each 
other until the group formed

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:50.670
are somehow moving 
towards a common goal.

00:21:56.530 --> 00:21:59.490
They're a group of people 
with different styles of thinking,

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:03.250
past experiences, 
and dreams for the future.

00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:09.010
But now they have to face the wall 
that's in front of them together.

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:13.240
<b>You can do it!</b>

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:12.520
Idols truly are mysterious...

00:22:13.530 --> 00:22:14.970
To be continued

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:47.460
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:48.290
I think I'm too ambitious.

00:23:48.290 --> 00:23:49.000
Is that right?

00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:51.230
I want to be the best idol I can be.

00:23:51.230 --> 00:23:52.030
The best, huh?

00:23:52.030 --> 00:23:55.320
Send your encouragement to me, 
Miyu, the top idol candidate!

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:57.470
Don't use our broadcast 
to make personal announcements!

00:23:57.470 --> 00:23:59.750
The next episode is 
"Gateway to Success!"

00:23:57.470 --> 00:23:59.750
<b>"Gateway to Success"</b>
